cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the JOSS paper."
type: software
title: "bci-mi-decoder: A reproducible per-subject adaptive ensemble for binary motor-imagery EEG decoding"
abstract: >
  Open-source Python package for binary motor-imagery EEG decoding under a
  strict cross-validation protocol. Enumerates a small, pre-specified set of
  candidate pipelines (CSP, pyRiemann tangent-space, EEGNet, stacking
  meta-learners), selects the highest-CV pipeline per subject under a single
  fixed StratifiedKFold partition, and produces fold-bagged probabilistic
  predictions on a held-out test set in a single command.
authors:
